Names: tsuzuki was developed under the working name "egemma". The embedding
engine's internal names (egemma_server, egemma_native, egemma_ref, egemma-cli,
EGEMMA_* variables) keep that name. "EmbeddingGemma" and "Gemma" are names of
Google's models. This project is an independent, unofficial implementation and
is not affiliated with or endorsed by Google.

Third-party material and attributions
-------------------------------------

1. Hugging Face Transformers (Apache License 2.0)
   https://github.com/huggingface/transformers  (v5.19.0)
   reference/egemma_ref/config.py and reference/egemma_ref/model.py re-implement,
   from scratch and with line citations, the configuration derivation and forward
   pass of models/embedding_gemma2/{configuration,modeling}_embedding_gemma2.py,
   modeling_rope_utils.py, and the processor's special-token rule
   (processing_utils.py, tokenization_utils_base.py). The C++/Metal engine
   (native/) reproduces the same numerical behavior. No source file is copied.

2. vLLM (Apache License 2.0)
   https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm  (commit 1dfe9fb)
   vllm/model_executor/models/embedding_gemma2.py is cited as a second source for
   the per-layer-embedding and attention details in reference/egemma_ref/model.py.

3. FlashAttention (paper: Dao et al., 2022, https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.14135)
   The tiled online-softmax attention in native/kernels.metal follows the
   published algorithm. No code is copied.

4. Apple Metal Performance Primitives (Apple SDK)
   The optional MPP matmul path (native/kernels.metal, EGEMMA_MPP) calls
   mpp::tensor_ops::matmul2d as documented in the macOS SDK header
   MPPTensorOpsMatMul2d.h. The framework is provided by the operating system and
   is not redistributed.

5. DeepSeek Harness / Cordis (MIT License)
   https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness  (dsh-v0.2.1-alpha.2)
   The dsh-plugins/ packages follow the documented Service Definition /
   Service Provider pattern and the request/spec split of @deepseek-ai/dsh-shell.
   @deepseek-ai/cordis, @deepseek-ai/schemastery, and @deepseek-ai/dsh-subprocess
   are peer dependencies supplied by the dsh installation and are not bundled.

6. LongMemEval (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2024 Di Wu)
   https://github.com/xiaowu0162/LongMemEval
   The evaluation scripts (scripts/eval/) grade answers with LongMemEval's official
   per-question-type judge prompts; the MIT license text is recorded with them in
   results/eval/memory/longmemeval-g1-judge.json. The dataset is not redistributed:
   only question IDs, hashes and aggregate scores are committed.

